      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the walk this message describes is already in aosp/4390445: `p3s_anon_rmap_range()` widens the anon_vma lookup of a small folio by three page offsets on either side of its index, and `p3s_anon_rmap_skip()` starts the walk in each 4KB anonymous VMA at its part of the window (`vma_anon_slice_window()`). So after an `mprotect()`, `munmap()` or naming split, reclaim, migration and `collect_procs_anon()` already find every VMA of the window. I couldn\u0027t find a case they miss either: a 4KB `mremap()` keeps the slice (see `include/linux/p3s/mremap.h`), and `UFFDIO_MOVE` only moves whole folios.\n\nAs far as I can see, what this patch adds is the native-tree check in `p3s_anon_rmap_range()`. That looks right to me: `fork()` copies the page size (`mm_dup_mmap()`) and `execve()` starts a new mm, so all VMAs of one anon_vma tree share it.\n\nCould you rewrite the subject and message around that? Something like \"ANDROID: P3S: mm: rmap: Keep the exact anon_vma lookup in native trees\", saying what it saves: walks in native trees no longer visit the VMAs that the wider lookup finds and then skips.",
